    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nBuilding Neovim with `zig build` on macOS currently produces an `nvim` binary that cannot load FFF.nvim's native Lua module.\n\nFFF.nvim fails because its Rust/Lua shared library depends on the Lua C API symbol `lua_tothread`, but the Zig-built `nvim` executable does not export `_lua_tothread`.\n\nThis appears to affect native Lua modules loaded with `package.loadlib` / `require`, not just FFF.nvim specifically.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOn macOS arm64:\n\n```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/neovim/neovim\ncd neovim\nzig build -Doptimize=ReleaseFast -Dtarget=aarch64-macos-none\n```\n\nInstall FFF.nvim, then run Neovim with FFF on the runtimepath and load its native module. For example:\n\n```sh\nzig-out/bin/nvim --headless -u NONE \\\n  +'set rtp+=/path/to/fff.nvim' \\\n  +'lua require(\"fff.rust\")' \\\n  +qa\n```\n\nAlternatively, launching a normal config that loads FFF.nvim triggers the same failure.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nFFF.nvim fails to load:\n\n```text\nFailed to load fff rust backend.\nError: Error loading library from .../fff.nvim/target/release/libfff_nvim.dylib:\ndlopen(.../libfff_nvim.dylib, 0x0006): symbol not found in flat namespace '_lua_tothread'\n```\n\nRunning FFF.nvim's downloader/build helper also reports the same missing symbol:\n\n```text\nDownloaded binary is not valid:\ndlopen(.../libfff_nvim.dylib.tmp, 0x0006): symbol not found in flat namespace '_lua_tothread'\n```\n\nThe Zig-built executable also does not appear to export that symbol:\n\n```sh\nnm -gU zig-out/bin/nvim | rg '_lua_tothread'\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNative Lua modules loaded by Neovim should be able to resolve documented Lua/LuaJIT C API symbols from the host process. FFF.nvim should load successfully with a Zig-built Neovim binary, as it does with regular Neovim builds.\n\n### Environment\n\n```text\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-7523+gf836b47d77\nBuild type: zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseFast -Dtarget=aarch64-macos-none\nLuaJIT 2.1.1774896198\nZig 0.16.0\nmacOS Darwin arm64\nFFF.nvim commit 960e689\n```\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
